// Tracked wrapper so a clean checkout (no cloud credentials) still generates and builds.
//
// CloudPushSecrets.xcconfig is gitignored and user-created (template:
// CloudPushSecrets.example.xcconfig). It carries the hosted-compute defaults baked into the app at
// build time:
//   NOOP_PUSH_ENDPOINT             — the Supabase Edge Function base (…/functions/v1/push)
//   NOOP_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  — the Supabase PUBLISHABLE key (`sb_publishable_…`). Public by design;
//                                    it identifies the project to Supabase Auth. It is the only Supabase
//                                    key the app may hold: never put a secret / service-role key here.
//   NOOP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY         — DEPRECATED legacy anon JWT; read only as a fallback for the
//                                    publishable key while a project still issues one.
//   NOOP_SOURCE_REVISION           — the deployed worker/source revision, for diagnostics
//   NOOP_FINAL_HOSTED_COMPUTE      — YES for a build that must run cloud-only: sync is on whenever the build is
//                                    configured, with no toggle, no opt-out, no endpoint override and a
//                                    sign-in that cannot be skipped. NO leaves cloud as an opt-in.
//   NOOP_ALLOW_LEGACY_ENROLLMENT   — YES only for a migration build whose phones still hold a NARA
//                                    enrollment-code credential and must keep using it until sign-in.
//                                    NO (the default) ignores any such credential.
//   NOOP_LEGACY_FLEET_TOKEN        — the shared fleet token of the legacy enrollment path. Ignored unless
//                                    NOOP_ALLOW_LEGACY_ENROLLMENT is YES. Empty in every tester build.
// When the secrets file is absent every $(NOOP_*) reference below resolves to an empty string, so the
// build has no receiver, `CloudPushSettings.isConfigured` is false, and the app behaves exactly like
// offline NOOP: no endpoint, no sign-in, no uploads, no cloud-mode toggle.
//
// Testers authenticate with Supabase Auth (email + password, emailed one-time code). The app then
// provisions its own per-account installation credential from that verified session, so nothing in this
// file is a per-user secret and nothing here can act as a user.
//
// NB: xcconfig parses "//" as a comment — a URL in a secrets file must be written as https:/$()/…
NOOP_PUSH_ENDPOINT =
NOOP_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY =
NOOP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =
NOOP_SOURCE_REVISION = development
NOOP_FINAL_HOSTED_COMPUTE = NO
NOOP_ALLOW_LEGACY_ENROLLMENT = NO
NOOP_LEGACY_FLEET_TOKEN =
// Sentry DSN (crash/hang/slow-transaction reporting). Empty disables Sentry. Set in CloudPushSecrets.xcconfig
// using https:/$()/ for the scheme. Public-by-design ingest key, not an auth token.
NOOP_SENTRY_DSN =
#include? "CloudPushSecrets.xcconfig"
